silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_02_twelve_leg_deep_dive_sections_01_record_leg_decomposition_step__step_record_leg_arrow a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "record_leg is the evidence/aboutness arrow from VetRecord_77 to MittensColimitApex. VetRecord_77 is an information object; MittensColimitApex is the individual. The arrow names the aboutness relation." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_02_twelve_leg_deep_dive_sections_01_record_leg_decomposition_step__step_monic_arrow_monomorphism a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The record_leg arrow is monic: if two distinct records VetRecord_77 and VetRecord_78 both map to Mittens via the record_leg, they are distinct records (not the same object). The monicity prevents record-conflation." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_02_twelve_leg_deep_dive_sections_01_record_leg_decomposition_step__step_about_ness_typed_english_olog_arrow__spivak_kent_§3 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Spivak-Kent ologs (§3): every olog arrow corresponds to a typed English sentence of the form '[source] [arrow] [target]'. For the record leg: 'VetRecord_77 is about MittensColimitApex'. The arrow is the grammatical relation 'is about'." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_02_twelve_leg_deep_dive_sections_01_record_leg_decomposition_step__step_vetrecord_77 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "VetRecord_77 is the concrete record node: the electronic health record for Mittens (microchip ID 44B2F9) created at the Tartu Animal Clinic on 2026-05-18, containing blood panel, weight measurement, species type, SHACL validation receipt, and audit trail." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_02_twelve_leg_deep_dive_sections_01_record_leg_decomposition_step__step_yoneda_inheritance_of_record_leg_type a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda naturality, every downstream paper that references Mittens's evidence must preserve the record-leg type: a health record is an aboutness node with a monic arrow to Mittens; treating the record as Mittens is the cheese-trap face 4 collapse. Paper 15 (KG growth) inherits this: KG nodes for health records must carry an aboutness arrow to the Mittens node, not an identity arrow." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_02_twelve_leg_deep_dive_sections_01_record_leg_decomposition_step__step_record_leg_recap a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The record_leg arrow VetRecord_77 -> MittensColimitApex is the typed about-ness arrow; it is monic (records are distinct); VetRecord_77 is not Mittens (cheese-trap face 4 block); downstream papers inherit the record-leg type via Yoneda naturality." .
